<!--
  Wazuh agent input for the audit sink. Runs on the VM HOST (not in the jail),
  pasted inside <ossec_config> in /var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf. The Wazuh
  counterpart of the [INPUT] in deploy/gatte-audit-fluentbit.conf; install and
  checks are in deploy/gatte-audit-wazuh.md.

  The path is the sink as the host sees it: the jail is a directory on the
  host. The file is 0600 owned by the gateway's service user, so it is read by
  wazuh-logcollector, which runs as root. Do not widen the mode to make
  another reader work.

  log_format json: one JSON object per line, decoded by Wazuh's stock JSON
  decoder, so every key of the line (hash, prev_hash, chain, type, ...) is a
  field. The raw line is kept as full_log.

  only-future-events no: after an agent restart, read what was written while
  it was down instead of skipping to the end. A skipped stretch is a gap in
  the chain as the SIEM sees it.
-->
<localfile>
  <log_format>json</log_format>
  <location>/usr/local/bastille/jails/gatte/root/var/log/mcp-gateway/audit.jsonl</location>
  <only-future-events>no</only-future-events>
</localfile>
